-- title:
--   Endomorphism classifying the norm bundle realises T_ℓ on points
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a natural number $M \neq 0$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ with $K =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $\operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise embedding [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ the fraction field of $A$, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with the tower $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero whose image in $\operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Write $c =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) for the structure morphism of the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) (a pushout of the spectra of the two chart algebras) over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, assumed proper.
--
--   *Relative $\operatorname{Pic}^0$ data.* Let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $c$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ (a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} A \to$ the model whose composite with $c$ is the identity), let $D$ be a `RelativePic0Designation` for $c$, i.e. a scheme $D.P$ with a structure morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and a zero section, and let `hrep` assert that the type of data exhibiting $D$ as representing the subfunctor of rigidified line bundles on $c$ satisfying the fibrewise algebraic-triviality condition `algEquivZeroCut` is nonempty. The morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is assumed smooth (`hsm`) and separated (`hsep`).
--
--   *Base-change hypotheses.* Compatible $A$- and $L$-algebra structures on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` are fixed. The base change of $c$ to $L$ is assumed smooth of relative dimension $1$ (`hsmL`) and geometrically integral (`hgiL`), and the base change $\operatorname{pullback.snd} D.\mathrm{toBase}\ (\operatorname{specMap} A\,L)$ of $D$ to $L$ is assumed proper (`hprL`) and geometrically connected (`hgcL`).
--
--   *The geometric fibre as a curve model.* Let $M_\eta$ be a `CurveModel` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ for the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182), i.e. an integral proper smooth relative-dimension-one curve over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with a specified isomorphism of its function field with that field and a bijection between its closed points and the places of that field; let $e_\eta$ be an isomorphism from $M_\eta.C$ to the base change of the two-chart model to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`heη`). The chart open obtained as the preimage of the image of the finite chart under $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection is assumed nonempty, and `hMηpin` pins the identification: for every element $a$ of the finite chart algebra over $K$, transporting along $M_\eta.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$ the germ at the generic point of the image of $a$ on that chart open gives the element of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the Laurent series of $a$ under $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The hypothesis `hgal` is the Galois equivariance of this identification: for every $g \in \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ fixing $L$ pointwise and all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x'$ of $M_\eta.C$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, if $x'$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ followed by $x$, $e_\eta$ and the first projection, then $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x' =$ [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (x1FunctionField (M * p)) g`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) $\cdot\, M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x$.
--
--   *Hecke and diamond inputs.* `hin` is [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsAll (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L58) (the Hecke input packages at all primes together with, for each $d$ coprime to $Mp$, the existence of a diamond automorphism of the function field and of a base-changed automorphism over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$), and `hcomm` is [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondCommuteBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L54), the commutation of the diamond generators over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. A semiring action of $L \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} L$ on $A$ is fixed, compatible with $A \to L$ (`hΓA`).
--
--   *The points dictionary.* Let `gpts` be a bijection from $J_1(Mp) = \operatorname{Pic}^0$ of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ onto the set of morphisms $\operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to D.P$ over $\operatorname{specMap} A\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, additive for the relative group law on $D$ coming from `hrep.some` and the group cut `algEquivZeroGroupCut` (`hgadd`).
--
--   *The Abel–Jacobi data.* `hDL` exhibits the base change $D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,L$ as representing the corresponding subfunctor for the base change of $c$ to $L$ with the base-changed section, and `hPL` asserts that its Poincaré bundle is isomorphic to the base change along `BaseChange.ofR` of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep.some` along the first projection from the $L$-base change of $D$. Let $\mathrm{ajL}$ be a morphism from the $L$-base change of the curve to that of $D$ over $L$ with $\varepsilon$ mapping to the zero section (`hajLε`), satisfying the Abel–Jacobi property `hajL`: for every field $K'$, every $t : \operatorname{Spec} K' \to \operatorname{Spec} L$ and every point $x$ of the base-changed curve over $t$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` along $x$ followed by $\mathrm{ajL}$ is isomorphic to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of the point $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of $t$ followed by the base-changed $\varepsilon$; thus it classifies $\mathcal{O}(x - \varepsilon)$. Let $k_L$ be the comparison morphism from the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change to the $L$-base change of the two-chart model, characterised by `hkL₁` and `hkL₂` through the two projections. Let $\overline{\mathrm{aj}} : M_\eta.C \to D.P$ be given by `hajbar` as $e_\eta$ followed by $k_L$, by $\mathrm{ajL}$ and by the first projection, with `hajbar_over` stating that it lies over $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$ followed by $\operatorname{specMap} A\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $\overline{\varepsilon}$ be a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $M_\eta.C$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which induces $\varepsilon$ (`hεbar`) and is carried to the zero section by $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ (`hεbar_aj`). Finally `hpts_aj` normalises `gpts` against $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$: for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, s$ of $M_\eta.C$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $s$ inducing $\varepsilon$, there is a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ on `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` equal to $\mathrm{single}(\mathrm{place}(x),1) - \mathrm{single}(\mathrm{place}(s),1)$ whose class satisfies $(\mathrm{gpts}(\mathrm{Pic0.mk}\,D_v)).1 = x \circ \overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ in diagrammatic order, namely $x$ followed by $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$.
--
--   *The degeneracy pair at $\ell$.* Let $\ell$ be a prime. Let $K_\ell =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ (M * p) (M * p * ℓ))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) carry compatible $A$-algebra and tower structures, and let $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ be nonzero with Laurent series [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Let $\pi_\alpha, \pi_\beta$ be morphisms over $A$ from the two-chart model of $(K_\ell, j_\ell)$ to that of $(K, j)$, both finite and locally of finite presentation, and let $\iota_\alpha, \iota_\beta$ be $A$-algebra maps between the corresponding finite chart algebras. Let $U$ be an open of the two-chart model over $K$. The hypotheses on this pair are: surjectivity of $\pi_\alpha$ and $\pi_\beta$ on points (`hsurjα`, `hsurjβ`); the $q$-expansion pins `hια` (the Laurent series of $\iota_\alpha b$ equals that of $b$) and `hιβ` (the Laurent series of $\iota_\beta b$ is [`ModularCurve.qExpand L ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25) applied to that of $b$); the commuting chart squares `hsqα`, `hsqβ` relating $\pi_\alpha$, $\pi_\beta$ with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\iota_\alpha$, $\iota_\beta$ and the finite chart immersions; chart preservation `hpreα`, `hpreβ`, stating that the preimage of the open range of the finite chart immersion is the open range of the finite chart immersion upstairs; `hUdim`, that every point of the model whose stalk has Krull dimension at most $1$ lies in $U$; flatness over $U$ (`hflα`, `hflβ`); and constancy of the rank over $U$ (`hrkα`, `hrkβ`): at every point of $U$ the finrank of $\pi_\alpha$, respectively $\pi_\beta$, equals $\ell$ if $\ell \mid Mp$ and $\ell + 1$ otherwise.
--
--   *The norm module and the endomorphism.* Let $\mathcal{N}$ be an invertible module on the product of the curve with $D$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ (the pullback of $c$ and $D.\mathrm{toBase}$), subject to `hNe`: for every open $V$ of that product and every $d'$, if the curve-change morphism induced by $\pi_\alpha$ restricted over $V$ is flat, locally of finite presentation and of finrank $d'$ at every point of $V$, then the restriction of $\mathcal{N}$ to $V$ is isomorphic to `Scheme.Modules.normModule` of that restricted morphism in degree $d'$ — the determinant of the pushforward tensored with the dual determinant of the pushforward of the unit — applied to the restriction to the preimage of $V$ of the pullback along the curve-change morphism induced by $\pi_\beta$ of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep.some`. Let $T_\ell$ be an endomorphism of $D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ such that the pullback of the Poincaré bundle along $T_\ell$ is isomorphic to the rigidification `Scheme.Modules.rigidify` of $\mathcal{N}$ along the rigidifying section determined by $\varepsilon$ and the second projection (`hTℓ`), and such that $T_\ell$ is a homomorphism for the relative group law: for every scheme $T$, every $s : T \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ and all points $x, y$ of $D$ over $s$, composing the product of $x$ and $y$ with $T_\ell$ equals the product of the composites (`hTℓmul`).
--
--   *Conclusion.* With the Hecke-algebra module structure [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleOneBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L129) on $J_1(Mp)$ installed, for every $x \in J_1(Mp)$ the underlying morphism of $\mathrm{gpts}$ of [`ModularCurve.heckeGenOne ⟨ℓ, Fact.out⟩ • x`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L18) equals $(\mathrm{gpts}\,x).1$ followed by the underlying morphism of $T_\ell$. Thus, under the points dictionary, the action of the Hecke generator at $\ell$ on $J_1(Mp)$ is postcomposition with $T_\ell$.
--
--   This is the points half of the statement that the Hecke operator at $\ell$ is realised by an endomorphism of the scheme representing the relative $\operatorname{Pic}^0$ of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$: given a degeneracy pair at $\ell$ and an endomorphism classifying the norm along $\pi_\alpha$ of the $\pi_\beta$-pullback of the Poincaré bundle, the Abel–Jacobi dictionary reads that endomorphism as $T_\ell$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points. It is used in the existence statement for such endomorphisms at all primes and in the descent of $T_\ell$ past the components of the special fibre.
